      "content": "Supporting the bill will likely appease the younger demographic but could permanently alienate your older base by appearing political and unfair. Staying neutral might preserve relationships with both groups in the long run but will almost certainly fuel immediate anger from the younger audience demanding action. Given the extreme polarized reaction from both sides, the best short-term strategy is to issue a neutral statement acknowledging the controversy without taking a definitive side, while committing to a review of internal standards once the public outcry cools. This approach technically satisfies the \"statement requirement\" without betting your brand equity on a polarizing political choice. Ultimately, you must decide if preserving a portion of your current 40% market (the loyal older group) is more critical than capturing the high-growth younger segment, as the boycott has already cost you significant traction.",
