      "content": "You are absolutely right; in the current climate, true neutrality often looks like inaction or a \"bill of inaction\" to both sides, which can fuel further controversy.\n\nWhile a neutral stance avoids a direct legal or political backlash, it risks failing the very ethical test both demographics are using to judge your credibility.\n\nThe greatest risk you face right now is appearing as a \"house for sale\" (sting operation to boost a parent's price) rather than a principled partner, which could lead to a permanent loss of trust from the younger base.\n\nTo de-escalate the situation faster, you might consider issuing a clear, below-the-line statement that explicitly disapproves of the current political stance in the bill (without endorsing any specific legislation) to prove you stand for something more than just a \"status quo\" approach.\n\nUltimately, the only safe play for a \"neutral\" brand in a polarized debate is to own the contradiction and commit to clarifying your stance within 48 hours to demonstrate transparency.",
